  "inspection": {
    "question": "What is the bolt circle diameter, and where did that number come from?",
    "answered": true,
    "answer": "The NEMA 23 standard defines a **square bolt pattern** with a side length of **47.14\u202fmm** (per the lookup_standard result). It does **not** specify a circular bolt circle diameter. The four M5 clearance holes are placed at the corners of this 47.14\u202fmm square, with a hole spacing equal to the side length. If you need a circular approximation, the diagonal of the square (\u2248\u202f66.6\u202fmm) would be the distance between opposite holes, but this is not a standard term for NEMA 23 mounts.",
